    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177">

                <pb facs="0391" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/804d</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 12, 1917</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: After consultation with
                    Secretary Mc-Adoo today, and in line with our talk last evening, I have prepared
                    the enclosed telegram which Secretary McAdoo approves.</p>
                <p>If it meets with your approval will you be good enough to send it to the
                    telegraph office of the Department so that it can immediately be put upon the
                        wires?<anchor n="28" xml:id="d177-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d177-a1.xml" xpointer="d177-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d177-f1" n="28" xml:id="d177-f1-content">
                <p>On the same day President Wilson replied: “This has my entire approval.” For
                    correspondence previously printed concerning the Kaledin movement, see <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav01#pg_306">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1918, Russia, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 306</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav01#pg_322">322</ref>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >passim</hi>, and <ref target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_40">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >ii</hi>, pp. 40</ref>, <ref target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_587">587</ref>,
                        <ref target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_588">588</ref>, <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_601">601</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_603">603</ref>, <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_609">609</ref>, <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_611">611</ref>, <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav02#pg_650">650</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
